native.py reproduces the two-entry decoder registry from src/diffsinger_task.py
and avoids eager imports of unrelated training/vocoder modules. The acoustic
model, diffusion sampler and NSF-HiFiGAN computation are imported from the
pinned checkout, not reimplemented or converted to ONNX.

Model weights are not included. The official female-triplet demo checkpoint
prohibits commercial use and requires speaker attribution as described at:
https://github.com/openvpi/DiffSinger/releases/tag/v1.5.0
The demo explicitly selects only the opencpop speaker (speaker ID 0).
The community NSF-HiFiGAN vocoder weights have separate non-commercial terms:
https://openvpi.github.io/vocoders/
The experimental profile does not authorize commercial deployment.
